public-algo/

# macOS and editors leave "name 2.ext" copies behind; they compiled quietly
# once, as a second copy of a file whose whole point is that there is one.
# Scoped to the sources that are compiled or run by the tests: the old blanket
# rule also hid legitimate files anywhere else (a "Library 2.jpg" among the
# photographs, a "notes 3.md"), and a file git silently ignores is worse than a
# duplicate in a build.
src/**/* [0-9].*
test/**/* [0-9].*
web-app/src/**/* [0-9].*
algo-app/src/**/* [0-9].*
